WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.390 --> 00:00:05.959
As detail-oriented as Game of Thrones usually
is, the fantasy drama has featured not one

00:00:05.959 --> 00:00:10.400
but two immersion-breaking mistakes during
its final season on television.

00:00:10.400 --> 00:00:13.800
After spotting a stray coffee cup that was
accidentally left in a shot on the fourth

00:00:13.800 --> 00:00:19.360
episode of Thrones season 8, viewers noticed
yet another erroneous object in frame on the

00:00:19.360 --> 00:00:20.570
series finale.

00:00:20.570 --> 00:00:24.839
Weirdly enough, this embarrassing gaffe is
also beverage-based, making it seem like the

00:00:24.840 --> 00:00:28.240
crew on the final season of the show may have
had a bit of a drinking problem.

00:00:31.860 --> 00:00:33.280
Spoilers ahead!

00:00:33.280 --> 00:00:37.780
Following Daenerys Targaryen's fire-and-fury
siege of King's Landing that killed thousands

00:00:37.780 --> 00:00:42.079
of innocent people, Tyrion Lannister resigned
as her Hand and asked Jon Snow to find the

00:00:42.079 --> 00:00:46.860
strength to make a difficult decision that
would ensure the safety of the Seven Kingdoms:

00:00:46.860 --> 00:00:51.280
kill Dany so she doesn't harm anyone else
under the guise of "liberation."

00:00:51.280 --> 00:00:55.660
Fast forward a few weeks, and Tyrion emerges
for his trial - which turns into a meeting

00:00:55.660 --> 00:00:59.910
of the minds with members of the remaining
Great Houses of Westeros, who decide that

00:00:59.910 --> 00:01:03.999
they will now and forevermore choose the king
or queen.

00:01:03.999 --> 00:01:08.479
Just as Tyrion is walking up to everyone,
the camera flips perspective to show Samwell

00:01:08.479 --> 00:01:13.770
Tarly, Edmure Tully, and an unknown character
watching the last Lannister sibling approaching.

00:01:13.770 --> 00:01:17.810
Keep your eyes on Sam during this moment,
and you'll see a plastic water bottle near

00:01:17.810 --> 00:01:18.810
his foot.

00:01:18.810 --> 00:01:22.280
It's about half hidden behind his boot, but
it's definitely noticeable.

00:01:22.280 --> 00:01:26.130
Looks like actor John Bradley was getting
parched during Tyrion's big speech, which

00:01:26.130 --> 00:01:27.130
is understandable ...

00:01:27.130 --> 00:01:31.160
"Listening to talkers makes me thirsty."

00:01:36.300 --> 00:01:41.000
Later on in the scene, a second water bottle
can be spotted behind Ser Davos Seaworth.

00:01:41.000 --> 00:01:43.920
Must have been a hot day in the Dragon Pit.

00:01:43.920 --> 00:01:47.090
Plastic water bottles are obviously very out
of place in Westeros …

00:01:47.090 --> 00:01:51.630
"I'd skin you alive for wine.

00:01:51.630 --> 00:01:52.630
F--- water!"

00:01:52.630 --> 00:01:56.079
… and the first of the two errors stuck
out to tons of watchers at home.

00:01:56.079 --> 00:02:01.990
Just as viewers were split over Season 8 as
a whole, they were also divided Water Bottle-gate.

00:02:01.990 --> 00:02:02.990
One fan wrote.

00:02:02.990 --> 00:02:04.970
"Seven hells, they did it again.

00:02:04.970 --> 00:02:07.030
It's a plastic water bottle."

00:02:07.030 --> 00:02:11.231
Another was frustrated to the point of all-caps-tweeting
after spotting the plastic water bottle in

00:02:11.231 --> 00:02:12.849
frame, writing,

00:02:12.849 --> 00:02:13.849
"PLEASEEEEEEEEEE.

00:02:13.849 --> 00:02:16.650
THERE WAS A PLASTIC WATER BOTTLE IN THIS EPISODE.

00:02:16.650 --> 00:02:17.650
NOT AGAIN."

00:02:17.650 --> 00:02:22.510
Voice actor Troy Hughes was equally as upset,
finding it hard to believe that the Game of

00:02:22.510 --> 00:02:25.390
Thrones crew could allow oversights like these
in the finale.

00:02:25.390 --> 00:02:26.670
He wrote,

00:02:26.670 --> 00:02:27.709
"Seriously!!!

00:02:27.709 --> 00:02:32.720
It's the finale of #GameOfThrones … EVERYBODY
is watching … and you leave a water bottle

00:02:32.720 --> 00:02:33.959
on the set?!?!"

00:02:33.959 --> 00:02:38.750
CBS Sports writer Will Brinson felt that the
bottle blunder was a microcosm of the last

00:02:38.750 --> 00:02:39.940
two seasons of Thrones.

00:02:39.940 --> 00:02:40.940
He tweeted,

00:02:40.940 --> 00:02:45.780
"Game of Thrones leaving a plastic water bottle
sitting there in the finale is such perfect

00:02:45.780 --> 00:02:50.700
symbolism for a show that spent the last two
seasons rushing to get done and ignoring the

00:02:50.700 --> 00:02:54.190
important little details that made it great
in the first place."

00:02:54.190 --> 00:02:57.170
Conversely, plenty of others thought that
the mistake was ultimately harmless.

00:02:57.170 --> 00:02:58.180
One viewer tweeted,

00:02:58.180 --> 00:03:01.470
"First a Starbucks coffee cup and now a water
bottle.

00:03:01.470 --> 00:03:02.550
I love it!

00:03:02.550 --> 00:03:03.629
[It's] super silly!"

00:03:03.629 --> 00:03:07.580
Another joked that HBO must have secured a
couple of sponsorships for the final season

00:03:07.580 --> 00:03:08.580
of Game of Thrones:

00:03:08.580 --> 00:03:11.230
"Let's all clap for the sponsors of this season.

00:03:11.230 --> 00:03:14.110
The plastic water bottle and the Starbucks
cup."

00:03:14.110 --> 00:03:18.459
Someone else even defended the Game of Thrones
team, noting that "framing isn't easy" and

00:03:18.459 --> 00:03:22.220
the crew might have been paying closer attention
to the actors' performances, the lighting,

00:03:22.220 --> 00:03:26.330
and the costumes than whether there were any
water bottles visible in the shot.

00:03:26.330 --> 00:03:30.439
For some fans, everything that was supposed
to be included in the Game of Thrones finale

00:03:30.439 --> 00:03:34.220
is more than enough to make them forget about
the out-of-place beverage.

00:03:34.220 --> 00:03:37.881
For others, the water bottle mishap serves
as another nail in the coffin of a season

00:03:37.881 --> 00:03:40.280
they weren't all that satisfied with.

00:03:40.280 --> 00:03:44.680
Like Tyrion said during his rousing finale
monologue, there's nothing more powerful in

00:03:44.680 --> 00:03:49.110
the world than a good story - but there's
nothing that can tarnish a tale like Game

00:03:49.110 --> 00:03:52.530
of Thrones as easily as an absent-minded slip-up.

